          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01VqviPw9PuBczHj7BNwBpH2",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022: \u0022concepts/single-composition-point.md\u0022, \u0022content\u0022: \u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Single Composition Point\\ndescription: How credential scoping and runtime-path resolution converge on one startup configuration point for security and maintainability.\\ntimestamp: 2025-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - source-type/synthesis\\n  - concept/Single-Composition-Point\\n  - tech/dotnet\\nconfidence: high\\nconfidence_reason: \\\u0022Both source pages explicitly describe their single-point decisions; the connection between them is direct and stated.\\\u0022\\nreview_date: 2026-01-14\\n---\\n\\nBoth credential-scoping and runtime-path resolution decisions converge on a single\\nprinciple: control the injection of external state into the system at one known point,\\nearly in the startup sequence, never scattered throughout the codebase.\\n\\n[[credential-scoping]] ensures that the Anthropic API key reaches only the specific child\\nprocess that needs it\u2014never the Hub\u0027s own environment\u2014by loading the secret at startup\\nand injecting it immediately before spawning the agent. This prevents a compromised Hub\\nprocess from leaking the credential through its own environment inspection.\\n\\n[[runtime-paths]] enforces the same discipline for file-system locations: every location\\nthe Hub uses at runtime is resolved in exactly one path resolver at startup, validated,\\nand then consumed downstream. No part of the codebase is allowed to rediscover paths on\\nits own or read the ambient working directory directly.\\n\\nBoth decisions share the same architectural intent: **centralize composition decisions**\\nso they can be audited, tested, and changed in one place without risk of logic scattering\\ninto the implementation. For credentials, this tightens the security perimeter; for paths,\\nit simplifies operations and makes the runtime configuration explicit and reproducible.\\n\u0022}"
